Build a beautiful, responsive web app called "RoomReimagine" — an AI
interior makeover portal where users upload a photo of their room, pick a
design style, and see an AI-restyled version of their own room. Use React
+ Vite + Tailwind CSS. For now use MOCK data and placeholder images
(https://picsum.photos seeds are fine) — no backend wiring yet; structure
data access behind a small mock service layer so Supabase can replace it
later without touching components.

DESIGN SYSTEM (apply consistently everywhere):
- Mood: warm, calm, editorial — like a premium interior design magazine,
  not a SaaS dashboard.
- Colors: background warm off-white #FAF7F2; surfaces white; ink
  #2B2622 for headings, #6B6259 for body; accent terracotta #C4704B for
  primary actions and active states; secondary sage #8A9B8E for badges
  and success; error #B3564D. No pure black, no cold grays, no blue.
- Typography: elegant serif for display headings (e.g. "Fraunces" or
  "Playfair Display" from Google Fonts), clean sans for UI and body
  (e.g. "Inter"). Generous line-height, large airy headings.
- Shape: rounded-2xl cards, soft warm shadows (shadow color derived from
  the ink tone at low opacity), 1px warm borders #EDE6DC where needed.
- Spacing: roomy — min 24px card padding, clear vertical rhythm.
- Imagery is the hero: room photos always displayed large with rounded
  corners; UI chrome stays quiet around them.
- Motion: subtle — 150-250ms ease transitions on hover/press, gentle
  fade/slide on screen enter. Nothing bouncy.
- Mobile-first: every screen must look intentional at 375px; nav
  collapses to a thumb-friendly bottom bar on small screens.

APP SHELL:
Header with a serif "RoomReimagine" wordmark, nav links "New Makeover"
and "Gallery" with a terracotta active underline, and an avatar menu with
Sign out. Bottom tab bar on mobile (New Makeover / Gallery).

SCREENS & ROUTES (build all, with mock state toggles I can preview):

1. /signin — Auth page. Split layout on desktop: left panel is a
   full-bleed hero collage of a room before/after with the tagline
   "See your room, reimagined." over a soft gradient; right panel holds
   the card with Sign In / Sign Up tabs, email + password fields with
   inline validation, a terracotta primary button with loading state,
   and friendly error messages. Mobile: hero shrinks to a compact
   banner above the card.

2. /new-makeover — The creation flow, one column, three steps visually
   numbered:
   Step 1 "Your room": large drag-and-drop upload zone (dashed warm
   border, camera icon, "Drop a photo or tap to choose"), with a
   preview state showing the chosen photo, a "Change photo" text
   button, and the tip "Use a well-lit, wide-angle photo for best
   results."
   Step 2 "Pick a style": a grid of 8 selectable style cards (2 cols
   mobile, 4 desktop), each with a thumbnail, name, and one-liner:
   Scandinavian, Modern Minimalist, Industrial, Bohemian, Japandi,
   Mid-Century Modern, Coastal, Rustic. Selected card gets a
   terracotta border + check chip.
   Step 3 "Make it yours (optional)": a notes input, max 200 chars
   with counter, placeholder "e.g., keep the sofa, add plants, warm
   lighting."
   Sticky footer bar with a large "Generate Makeover" primary button,
   disabled with helper text until photo + style are set.

3. /result/:id — The reveal. Two mock states I can toggle:
   LOADING: the uploaded room photo dimmed with a slow shimmer sweep
   and rotating status lines ("Analyzing your room…", "Applying Japandi
   style…", "Rendering your makeover…") and the style badge.
   COMPLETE: a large before/after compare slider (draggable divider
   with a round handle, "Before"/"After" labels, style badge top-left),
   a Before/After toggle button beneath, the notes as a caption, and an
   action bar: "Save to Gallery" (primary), "Try Another Style"
   (secondary). Also design a FAILED state: warm, encouraging message
   "That one didn't work — let's try again" with a Retry button.

4. /gallery — Personal gallery. Masonry-ish responsive card grid
   (2 cols mobile / 3-4 desktop) of saved concepts: concept image,
   style badge, date, and a "{n} styles" sage chip when a room has
   multiple concepts. Include a designed EMPTY state: soft
   illustration or large emoji, "No makeovers yet", and a primary
   "Create your first makeover" button.

5. /concept/:id — Concept detail. The same compare slider component as
   /result reused at full width, style badge + notes + date, a "Style
   Shootout" section shown when the room has 2+ concepts (original
   photo card labeled "Original", then concept cards each with style
   badge, the current one outlined "Viewing", ending with a
   "+ Try Another Style" tile), and a quiet danger-styled Delete button
   with a confirmation dialog.

SHARED COMPONENTS (create once, reuse everywhere): PrimaryButton,
SecondaryButton (both with loading/disabled), Toast (success/error,
auto-dismiss), Spinner, CompareSlider, StyleBadge, EmptyState.

Include a hidden /dev route with links to every screen in every mock
state (loading/complete/failed/empty) so the design can be reviewed
end-to-end without a backend.

For all designs I ask you to make, have them be beautiful, not cookie cutter. Make webpages that are fully featured and worthy for production.

By default, this template supports JSX syntax with Tailwind CSS classes, React hooks, and Lucide React for icons. Do not install other packages for UI themes, icons, etc unless absolutely necessary or I request them.

Use icons from lucide-react for logos.

Import project modules with the `@/` path alias, which maps to `src/` (e.g. `@/components/Foo` == `src/components/Foo`), instead of deep relative paths like `../../components/Foo`.
